# Plots gallery checklist

`/plots` is the mock-data gallery for visual design (no R). When you add or materially change a chart, update the gallery in the same change.

## Required

1. Add or update a fixture in `app/src/fixtures/p1Gallery.ts` (or a sibling fixture module if the gallery grows).
2. Ensure `PlotsGalleryRoute` renders it (fixtures are mapped from `p1GalleryFixtures` today).
3. Use plain props + `moduleReady={false}` — never wire the gallery to Rserve/widget hooks.
4. Prefer cropping to the relevant pane (`P1Crop` pattern) over adding `show`/`paneCount` props to the display shells unless product UI needs that.

## What counts as a “new chart”

- A new population / sample / distribution visual variant (e.g. new `variableSupport`, statistic, or group layout).
- A new drawing path in `ThreePaneDisplay`, `ProportionThreePaneDisplay`, or `d3/*` that produces a distinct P1 (or later P2/P3) look.

## Out of scope

- Pure animation timing tweaks with no visual structure change.
- Control-panel / routing / R plumbing only.

## Example

```ts
// app/src/fixtures/p1Gallery.ts
export const p1GalleryFixtures = [
  // …existing
  buildOneNum('iqr'), // ← new visual variant gets a fixture
]
```

Verify at `/plots` without starting R.
